163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (FinOps for AI still manages cost the way traditional FinOps always has: after a system is deployed, through observability and correction. The Foundation's own 2026 Framework calls for shifting that work left, into design and architecture, but even its current "Architecting & Workload Placement" capability stops at the architecture of the AI system itself \(orchestration, inference, RAG\), not the architecture of the project that system is building. This deck argues for shifting further: treating the Software Engineering practice around it as cost-architecture decisions made before a single feature is written, using a real project, Spiresen Saga, as the working proof.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
